 "notes": [
  {
   "id": 4314821235,
   "type": "DiffNote",
   "body": "![kody code-review](https://img.shields.io/badge/kody-code--review-312B4B?labelColor=C9BBF2) ![Bug](https://img.shields.io/badge/Bug-B71C1C) ![high](https://img.shields.io/badge/severity_level-high-6B6B92)\n\n\n**enroll() decrements remainingSeats without checking class capacity**\n\nDecrementing `remainingSeats` without a capacity check drives it negative and oversubscribes the class. Reject the enrollment when `seats > enrollment.remainingSeats` before saving.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for LLM</summary>\n\n````text\nFile apps/api/src/report-cards/qa2576/report-card.service.ts, lines 42-45:\n\nenroll() decrements remainingSeats without checking class capacity\n\n`remainingSeats` is decremented by `seats` without checking that enough seats remain, so enrolling into a full class drives `remainingSeats` negative and oversubscribes the class (e.g. remainingSeats=0, seats=1 -> -1). Reject the enrollment when `seats > enrollment.remainingSeats` before saving.\n\nSuggested code:\n\nconst enrollment = await this.enrollments.findOne({ where: { classId } });\nif (!enrollment) throw new NotFoundException('class not found');\nif (seats > enrollment.remainingSeats) throw new BadRequestException('not enough remaining seats');\nenrollment.remainingSeats = enrollment.remainingSeats - seats;\nawait this.enrollments.save(enrollment);\n````\n\n</details>\n\n\n<sub>Talk to Kody by mentioning @kody</sub>\n\n\n<sub>Was this suggestion helpful? React with \ud83d\udc4d or \ud83d\udc4e to help Kody learn from this interaction.</sub>\n\n<!-- kody-codereview -->&#8203;\n&#8203;",
   "created_at": "2026-11-24T19:11:57.165Z",
